      "error": null,
      "model": "deepseek-chat",
      "status": "ok",
      "summary": "Decision preview is BLOCK and must stand: the candidate Deployment sets DEMO_STARTUP_FAIL=true, a deliberate fault-injection value (FAULT_INJECTION, BLOCK). Trusted cases confirm this env var makes the new Pod print startup_failed and enter CrashLoop while the old Pod keeps serving, so it validates rollout protection rather than a healthy release; it must be rejected, not approved. The change also touches only gitops/demo/values.yaml with no Argo source/application change, so any rollback must be a Git revert plus Argo resync, not an imperative undo. Additional review items: 35 scheduled Pods lack CPU/memory requests, so free capacity (2190m CPU, ~9.2GB) may be overstated; KubeCPUOvercommit is firing; request_rate is 0, so zero errors/latency cannot be read as healthy; and the AI result status is invalid (ERROR)."
    },
